# Loops

> Loops is an email platform for software companies. Send transactional and marketing email from one API, one contact model, and a no-code visual editor, with a free tier that doesn't expire. Built for engineers and lifecycle teams who want both developer-grade APIs and marketer-friendly tools in one place.

- Website: https://loops.so
- Docs: https://loops.so/docs
- API reference: https://loops.so/docs/api-reference
- OpenAPI specification: https://app.loops.so/openapi.json
- MCP server: https://mcp.loops.so
- For AI agents: https://loops.so/agents (skills, CLI, llms.txt, MCP)
- Agent skills and plugin source: https://github.com/Loops-so/skills

## Email by type
- [Email API for developers](https://loops.so/email-api): REST email API with typed SDKs, webhooks, and lifecycle workflows. Transactional and marketing from one endpoint, with a free tier.
- [Marketing Email for Software Companies](https://loops.so/marketing-email): Send marketing campaigns using the same contact data as your product emails. Build audiences with segments and mailing lists in Loops.
- [Product & Lifecycle Email](https://loops.so/product-email): Send onboarding, trial, and re-engagement emails from product events. Keep contact data current and test workflow branches and exit conditions in Loops.
- [Transactional Email Service](https://loops.so/transactional-email): Send password resets, receipts, and login codes through Loops. Authenticate your domain, use published templates, and monitor transactional delivery.

## Features
- [Email Deliverability Software for SaaS](https://loops.so/deliverability): Loops signs every email with DKIM, monitors sends on the way out, and suppresses hard bounces and spam complaints. Copy your DNS records once and verify.
- [Email Editor with Themes and Components](https://loops.so/email-editor): Write and design emails in the Loops editor. Update a theme or component once and every email using it follows, and edit the same emails from code with LMX.
- [Email Conversion Tracking and Split Testing](https://loops.so/goals): Attach a goal to a Loops campaign and count the contacts who reach a target state, like upgrading to paid, within days you set. Split test emails in workflows.
- [Email Workflow Automation for SaaS](https://loops.so/workflows): Start email workflows from signups, property changes, or app events. Add timers, branches, audience filters, and experiments, or build them from the API.

## For AI agents and developers
- [Email for AI agents: CLI, API, MCP, and skills](https://loops.so/agents): Let Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and other coding agents install Loops, migrate an email stack, send events, and test transactional email.
- [Loops REST API for AI Agents: OpenAPI Spec](https://loops.so/agents/api): Explore the Loops REST API: contacts, events, transactional email, campaigns, workflows, themes, and more, with an OpenAPI spec for client generation.
- [Loops CLI: Manage Email from the Terminal](https://loops.so/agents/cli): Install the Loops CLI with Homebrew or curl and manage contacts, events, transactional email, and mailing lists from your terminal. Supports JSON output.
- [LMX: Loops Markup Extended for Email Content](https://loops.so/agents/lmx): LMX (Loops Markup Extended) is a semantic markup language for email. Author campaigns in code with the Content API and keep editing visually in Loops.
- [Loops MCP Server for AI Agents](https://loops.so/agents/mcp): Connect compatible Streamable HTTP MCP clients and Claude to Loops using browser OAuth. Manage contacts, lists, events, transactional email, and more.
- [Plan an Email Migration with AI Agents](https://loops.so/agents/migrate): Use the Loops API skill and migration guide to map contacts, events, templates, and transactional sends. The dedicated /migrate skill is coming soon.
- [Set Up Loops with an AI Agent](https://loops.so/agents/setup): Install the Loops API skill, then ask your agent to add an SDK or REST integration, create a contact, and send a test event. The /setup skill is coming soon.
- [Agent Skills for the Loops API, CLI, and LMX](https://loops.so/agents/skills): Install agent skills for the Loops API, CLI, LMX, and email sending best practices. Each skill adds focused Loops context to your coding agent.
- [Loops Workflows API: Create and Manage Workflows](https://loops.so/agents/workflows): Create, read, and update workflows, change mailing lists, and create, branch, update, or delete workflow nodes through the Loops API.

## Resources and guides
- [Email Resources: Guides, Examples & Glossary](https://loops.so/resources): Practical email guides, real examples, and a plain-English glossary from Loops. Learn deliverability, lifecycle, and marketing email, then see how to send it.
- [10 Best Email APIs for Developers](https://loops.so/resources/best-email-api-tools): Compare 10 email APIs by SDKs, templates, retries, webhooks, inbound routing, regional controls, and the sending operations your team needs to own.
- [12 Best Email Deliverability Tools for SaaS (2026)](https://loops.so/resources/best-email-deliverability-tools): Choose deliverability tools for the question you need to answer: whether authentication passes, how a mailbox provider rates your sending domain, where test messages arrive, or which addresses may be invalid.
- [10 Best Email Marketing Automation Platforms for SaaS](https://loops.so/resources/best-email-marketing-automation): Compare 10 SaaS email automation platforms by product-event triggers, workflow controls, channels, data model, and marketing and transactional email coverage.
- [Best Time to Send Email](https://loops.so/resources/best-time-to-send-email): Choose email send windows from audience behavior and published studies, then compare clicks or conversions. Test timing instead of assuming a universal best day.
- [Best Transactional Email Services: 8 Options Compared](https://loops.so/resources/best-transactional-email-services): Compare eight transactional email services by templates, delivery events, suppression handling, marketing features, and the operational work each requires.
- [Customer Engagement Tools: What They Are and 9 Options](https://loops.so/resources/customer-engagement-tools): A customer engagement tool is software that helps a company reach, message, and understand its users on the channels those users already use: email, in-app, push, chat, and support. Compare tools by the channels, data, and operating tasks your team needs.
- [Email A/B Testing: What to Test and How to Read Results](https://loops.so/resources/email-ab-testing): Test lifecycle emails with Loops Experiments, plan conversion windows and sample sizes, and estimate incremental activation lift with a randomized holdout.
- [Email Churn Rate](https://loops.so/resources/email-churn-rate): Calculate email churn using unique subscribers lost to unsubscribes, hard bounces, and complaints. Track inactivity and deliberate marketing pauses separately.
- [Email Deliverability Best Practices](https://loops.so/resources/email-deliverability): Check email authentication, sending reputation, audience consent, and message content. Distinguish delivery rate from inbox placement and investigate failures.
- [Email Marketing KPIs: The Metrics That Actually Matter](https://loops.so/resources/email-marketing-kpis): Measure SaaS email activation and paid upgrades, define attribution windows, use Loops Goals, and distinguish conversion reporting from incremental lift.
- [Email Marketing Laws](https://loops.so/resources/email-marketing-laws): What CAN-SPAM, GDPR, and CASL require, how to handle marketing opt-outs, and why required transactional email should remain separate.
- [Lifecycle Email: Triggers, Branches, and Exit Rules](https://loops.so/resources/lifecycle-email): Build SaaS lifecycle email for onboarding, trials, retention, and Stripe failed-payment recovery. Define triggers, reminder schedules, and current-state exits.
- [Migrate from Brevo to Loops](https://loops.so/resources/migrate-brevo-to-loops): Move Brevo email to Loops by mapping templates and API calls, preserving subscription and suppression state, and testing each send path before cutover.
- [Migrate from Customer.io to Loops](https://loops.so/resources/migrate-customerio-to-loops): Migrate Customer.io contacts, events, and emails to Loops with state reconciliation, suppression checks, pilot acceptance tests, and a rollback plan.
- [Migrate from Mailchimp to Loops](https://loops.so/resources/migrate-mailchimp-to-loops): Move Mailchimp email to Loops by mapping templates and API calls, preserving subscription and suppression state, and testing each send path before cutover.
- [Migrate from Mailgun to Loops](https://loops.so/resources/migrate-mailgun-to-loops): Move Mailgun email to Loops by mapping templates and API calls, preserving subscription and suppression state, and testing each send path before cutover.
- [Migrate from Postmark to Loops](https://loops.so/resources/migrate-postmark-to-loops): Move Postmark email to Loops by mapping templates and API calls, preserving subscription and suppression state, and testing each send path before cutover.
- [Migrate from SendGrid to Loops](https://loops.so/resources/migrate-sendgrid-to-loops): Migrate SendGrid email and contact lists to Loops. Map templates, preserve subscription state, handle retries, and verify each send path before cutover.
- [Send transactional email from Next.js](https://loops.so/resources/nextjs-transactional-email): Add transactional email to a Next.js app with the Loops SDK. Working code for signup sync and password reset emails, env setup, and a testing checklist.
- [Send transactional email from Node.js](https://loops.so/resources/node-transactional-email): Send transactional email from any Node.js app with the Loops SDK. Working code for your first send, error handling, retries, idempotency, and testing.
- [125 SaaS Email Examples Analyzed](https://loops.so/resources/saas-email-examples-benchmark): We analyzed 125 public SaaS email examples across 14 categories. See subject length, emoji use, punctuation, body length, and recipient language.
- [SaaS Email Program Audit: 14-Point Checklist](https://loops.so/resources/saas-email-program-audit): Review consent, sending identity, product data, lifecycle coverage, workflow safety, deliverability, and measurement. Use the evidence to choose the first repairs.
- [Send email from AI agents and coding assistants](https://loops.so/resources/send-email-from-ai-agents): Connect Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, or a compatible MCP client to Loops. Use the API, CLI, and agent skills to manage contacts, events, and email content.
- [Send a welcome email after signup with Loops](https://loops.so/resources/send-welcome-email-after-signup): Add a signup event and a Loops Workflow for one welcome email. Map current marketing permission, configure the message, and test retries and opt-outs before release.
- [SMTP Error Codes Explained: 421, 550, 554 and More](https://loops.so/resources/smtp-error-codes): An SMTP error code is the three-digit reply a receiving mail server sends back while it handles your message. The first digit tells you the category.
- [SMTP Ports, IMAP vs POP3, and Email Verification](https://loops.so/resources/smtp-ports-email-protocols): Compare SMTP ports 25, 587, and 465, IMAP, POP3, and email APIs. Match TLS settings to your provider and distinguish address validation from ownership verification.
- [Send Stripe failed payment and receipt emails](https://loops.so/resources/stripe-payment-emails): Send failed payment, dunning, and receipt emails from Stripe events. Compare Stripe built-in emails, the Loops Stripe app, and a webhook to the Loops API.
- [Transactional Email Best Practices for SaaS](https://loops.so/resources/transactional-email-best-practices): Build reliable transactional email for SaaS: message classification, authentication, stable retries, templates, security, suppressions, and delivery monitoring.
- [Why Are My Emails Going to Spam?](https://loops.so/resources/why-emails-go-to-spam): Investigate spam placement by checking authentication, audience permission, content, reputation, blocklists, unsubscribe handling, and volume changes. Use message headers and provider logs to identify which condition changed.

## Examples
- [Email Examples: Real SaaS Emails and Templates](https://loops.so/examples): Browse real email examples and templates from software companies: welcome, onboarding, transactional, and marketing emails you can adapt in Loops.
- [Account Verification Email Examples + Templates](https://loops.so/examples/account-verification-email-examples): See account verification email examples, subject lines, copy patterns, and templates for SaaS signup, login, and security flows.
- [Black Friday Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/black-friday-email-examples): See Black Friday email examples from SaaS companies like Typefully and Llama Life, with notes on the offers and CTAs in each one.
- [Email Footer Examples + Best Practices](https://loops.so/examples/email-footer-examples): See 12 real email footer examples with best practices and legal requirements SaaS teams can copy into Loops.
- [New Years Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/new-year-email-examples): See New Year email examples from SaaS companies like Buffer, Folk, and Reflect, with notes on how each recaps the year and previews what is next.
- [Notification Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/notification-email-examples): See notification email examples from Slack, Notion, Google, and Robinhood, covering trial endings, security alerts, and account updates.
- [Onboarding Emails: Examples, Sequences, and Templates](https://loops.so/examples/onboarding-email-examples): See eight SaaS onboarding email examples. Build a sequence around signup, activation, user role, and behavior. Stop setup nudges after activation.
- [Password Reset Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/password-reset-email-examples): See password reset email examples from Peloton and SeatGeek, with notes on the CTAs and security details that get users back into their accounts.
- [Payment Confirmation Email Examples + Templates](https://loops.so/examples/payment-confirmation-email-examples): See payment confirmation email examples and receipt templates, with subject lines and billing email tips SaaS teams can copy into Loops.
- [Privacy Policy Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/privacy-policy-and-terms-of-service-update-email-examples): See privacy policy and terms of service update email examples from Loom, Klarna, Reddit, and more, with notes on what makes each clear and trustworthy.
- [Product Hunt Launch Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/product-hunt-launch-email-examples): See Product Hunt launch email examples from Layers, Canny, and Polywork, with notes on how each one asks for support on launch day.
- [Product Update Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/product-update-email-examples): See product update email examples from Slack, Notion, Buffer, and more, with notes on how each one announces new features.
- [Survey Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/survey-email-examples): See survey email examples from Figma, Webflow, Uber, and Tesla, with notes on the subject lines and incentives in each one.
- [Waitlist Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/waitlist-email-examples): See waitlist email examples from Robinhood, Spline, and Loops, with notes on how each one sets expectations and keeps signups informed until launch.
- [Webinar Invitation Email Examples](https://loops.so/examples/webinar-invitation-email-examples): See webinar invitation email examples from Airtable, Calendly, DigiCert, and AWS, with notes on the subject lines and CTAs in each one.
- [Welcome Email Examples, Templates & Subject Lines](https://loops.so/examples/welcome-email-examples): See 17 real SaaS welcome email examples, subject-line options, templates, and a comparison table for choosing the right format.
- [Win-Back Email Examples + Campaign Ideas](https://loops.so/examples/win-back-email-examples): See win-back email examples and campaign ideas that re-engage inactive customers before they churn for good.

